Can your colleagues in production count on spotless and hygienic workspaces? Do you enjoy staying active on the job? Then you can quickly start working as a cleaner or industrial cleaner at Luiten! Your full-time workday starts around 9:00 or 10:00 AM. You’ll change into your work attire, grab your cleaning materials and equipment, and begin moving between the various production areas with your high-pressure cleaner.
Not only will you thoroughly clean the production spaces, but you’ll also ensure that the machines used to process and package meat—and all related materials—are meticulously cleaned. You take care of your own work, following HACCP and hygiene regulations carefully. In addition to cleaning, you make sure that every area is safe to enter and ready for use.
No need for an activity tracker here, as you’ll definitely get plenty of daily movement in this role! Together with your friendly, multicultural team, you’ll ensure production can start on time and in a clean environment.

- You are available full-time from Monday till Friday;
- Overtime doesn’t wear you out—instead, it makes your wallet fuller;
- You speak Dutch or English, essential for safety on the work floor;
- Some experience with cleaning and/or sanitation is a plus.

Do you enjoy being active and seeing tangible results? Are you looking for a job where you can work more hours by working at different locations? Then this combined role is perfect for you!
We offer you the opportunity to work at both the Designer Outlet Center in Roermond and De Leistert vacation park in Roggel. By combining these two locations, you can expect a workweek of approximately 32 to 40 hours.

What will you be doing?

You’ll be working at two different locations, which ensures plenty of variety in your work:

Designer Outlet Center Roermond

- Cleaning streets and plazas with street sweepers and pressure washers;
- Emptying trash cans on the premises;
- Picking up litter;
- Ensuring a clean and well-maintained environment for visitors.

De Leistert Holiday Park (Roggel)

- Cleaning bungalows, vacation homes, and restroom facilities;
- Making beds;
- Cleaning kitchens, bathrooms, bedrooms, and living rooms;
- Dusting and mopping the accommodations;
- Identifying and reporting any defects.

This combination offers a varied job where you work both indoors and outdoors and see the immediate results of your work.

Work Hours

- Outlet Roermond: flexible availability, including weekends;
- De Leistert: Mondays and Fridays between 9:00 AM and 3:00 PM (alternating days) with the possibility of additional work during the week;
- A combination of both locations allows for a workweek of approximately 32 to 40 hours.

- You’re a go-getter and enjoy being active;
- You’re available for at least 15 hours per week;
- You’re flexible (including weekends for the outlet);
- You’re available on Mondays and Fridays (for De Leistert);
- You speak Dutch, English, or German;
- Experience in cleaning is a plus, but not required.

You’ll ensure that goods are processed correctly, that drivers can continue their journeys quickly, and that customers know exactly where they stand.

In this role, you’ll combine customer contact with logistics administration and hands-on work on the shop floor.

You’ll be working for an international logistics service provider where goods arrive and are dispatched on a daily basis. As a Customer Service Assistant in Warehousing, you’ll act as the link between customers, drivers, warehouse staff and other departments. You’ll enter data into the warehouse systems, keep the records in order and ensure that the correct information is available to everyone involved in the logistics process.

In addition, you’ll support colleagues on the shop floor with queries about goods and orders. You’ll welcome drivers at the drivers’ desk, check freight documents and ensure that the necessary paperwork and data are in order. If something doesn’t go to plan, you’ll investigate what’s going on and liaise with the relevant colleagues to resolve the issue.

Your duties will include:

- Processing and recording incoming goods in the warehouse system;
- Checking and processing freight documents and other logistics administration;
- Welcoming and assisting drivers at the drivers’ desk and providing them with the correct information;
- Supporting warehouse staff with enquiries regarding goods, orders and records;
- Answering queries from customers and colleagues and resolving issues in the logistics process;
- Monitoring the progress of goods flows and ensuring data is processed correctly.

You will work Monday to Friday on day shifts from 08:30 to 17:00.

- You already have some demonstrable experience in a similar role within the logistics sector;
- You have strong communication skills and enjoy talking to customers and helping them;
- You are fluent in Dutch and/or English, both spoken and written;
- You are flexible, can cope with a hectic workload and are keen to develop your caree

Are you looking for a fulltime job in logistics? Would you like to work in a modern, international warehouse where fashion and clothing products are shipped to customers all over the world? Then this opportunity could be perfect for you!

For a large logistics clothing warehouse in Lelystad, we are looking for motivated Production Workers, Warehouse Operatives, and Logistics Associates. You will become part of a friendly international team where teamwork, quality, and a positive working atmosphere are key. On top of that, you can enjoy a delicious hot lunch every working day.

As a Production Worker in the warehouse, you will help ensure that all goods are processed efficiently and accurately. Your tasks will include:

- Loading and unloading trucks;
- Picking and packing customer orders;
- Checking products for quality;
- Unpacking boxes and processing incoming goods;
- Sorting clothing and accessories;
- Maintaining a clean and safe working environment.

This is a full-time position in a 2-shift rotation:

- Morning shift: 07:00 AM - 03:30 PM
- Afternoon shift: 03:00 PM - 11:30 PM

But there is also a nightshift you can work if you want from 23:00 tot 07:30. And there is work in the weekends!

- (Basic) English communication skills, or Polish or Spanish;
- Availability for full-time work in a 2-shift schedule;
- Ability to work effectively in a team;
- Physically fit and comfortable performing active warehouse work;
- Attention to detail and ability to follow instructions;
- Previous logistics or warehouse experience is a plus, but not required.
